Work order S1.3a-r3 (brief ALE_S1_3A_R3): the five open cells of tg_Z64_F --motion follow, step 150, frame Fh.
Dump: ../S1_3a_r2.f2.tg_Z64_F.1.dump (on disk, not committed).

Reproduction (one command, host, about 1 min at load 40):
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 OMP_PROC_BIND=false build_s2/tests/kokkos/test_ale_frame \
      --replay build_s2/gate_logs/S1_3a_r2.f2.tg_Z64_F.1.dump --repeat 1 --facets
  -> REPLAYCOLD: cells 1994 2106 6191 10177 10244 open (1.427e-03 max); REPLAYREPORT incomplete=549;
     REPLAYSTATUS status=4 (kIncomplete) on all five. Log ../S1_3a_r3.facets.host.log (GPU: .gpu.log, identical).
  The same with --window 5: open=0, maxOpenFrac 3.46e-14, incomplete=0 (../S1_3a_r3.facets.w5.host.log).

Truth (scipy):
  python tests/python/ale_truth_cells.py build_s2/gate_logs/S1_3a_r2.f2.tg_Z64_F.1.dump build_s2/gate_logs/S1_3a_r3.facets.host.log
  -> 2106 and 10177 miss each other (distance 4.672 h, beyond the gather window 4 h); the other three cells are
     exact to 1e-14 and open only through them (../S1_3a_r3.truth.log).
Distortion of a frame:
  python tests/python/ale_mesh_distortion.py DUMP   (../S1_3a_r3.distortion.log)

Cause: the cold build gathers candidates within kSearchWindow = 4 blocks (include/peclet/voro/params.hpp:28,
passed as `sw` to MovingTessellation::alloc by the tests); a cell with 2 r_max >= 4 blocks is flagged kIncomplete
(include/peclet/voro/tessellator.hpp:417, 464-465, covSq at :704) in MovingTessellation::lastStatus / report()
(include/peclet/voro/repair.hpp:164-178, 312), which ale/frame.hpp does not read.

Cure (option, no engine change): --window 6 for the follow runs (tools/ale_gates/G1_3.sh F2). Rerun of
tg_Z64_F --motion follow --tend 1 --window 6 on the GPU: DONE, 375 steps, gcl 9.93e-15, open_max 3.17e-13,
closure 3.96e-18, mom_booked 1.01e-17 (../S1_3a_r3.d2.tg_Z64_F.gpu.log). Time per frame, host 8 threads, load 47-50
(test_ale_frame N --part g --time --window W, ../S1_3a_r3.time.n*.w*.host.log): 32^3 w4 314-341 ms, w6 314-317 ms;
64^3 w4 2394-2465 ms, w6 2381-2435 ms: no difference above the noise. The window is not bitwise inert:
--part g at 32^3 rebuilt 866134 cells at w6 against 866136 at w4 (rounding-level differences).
